Read dictionaries from BDICT data instead of .aff/.dic files

Chromium ships Hunspell dictionaries as BDICT files
(third_party/hunspell_dictionaries/), read by the code in
third_party/hunspell/google/. Under HUNSPELL_CHROME_CLIENT, Hunspell takes
the BDICT bytes, AffixMgr and HashMgr take a hunspell::BDictReader instead of
file paths, SuggestMgr gets the reader too, FileMgr reads lines through a
LineIterator, HashMgr looks words up in the BDICT and caches the hentry
objects, and SuggestMgr uses the BDICT replacement table.

